# Custom Angis coding in your own language flow

Blueprint Player with name: Fell, score: 0, mood: focused.
Create Player named me with name: Fell Flow.
Create list named crate with beat, code, flow.
Create dictionary named profile with name: Fell Flow, language: Angis, mode: custom.

Teach Angis bless {target:name} with {amount:number} bars to do:
    Set, target.score to target.score + amount.
    Return, target.score.

When I say drop {line:text}, do:
    Show, "Fell Flow: " + line.

Teach Angis flex {message:text} to do Show, "Flex: " + message.
Teach Angis lock in {message:text} to do Show, "Locked: " + message.

Teach Angis stash {content:text} inside {path:path} to do:
    Write text content to file path as stashResult.
    Return, stashResult.

Teach Angis pull from {path:path} to do:
    Read file path as pulledText.
    Return, pulledText.

Teach Angis make tag from {message:text} to do:
    Slugify message as tagText.
    Return, tagText.

Teach Angis loud {message:text} to do:
    Set loudText to text uppercase with text: message.
    Return, loudText.

Teach Angis quiet {message:text} to do:
    Set quietText to text lowercase with text: message.
    Return, quietText.

Teach Angis swap {old:text} inside {source:text} with {new:text} to do:
    Replace old in source with new as swappedText.
    Return, swappedText.

Teach Angis count my {items:name} to do:
    Count length of items as itemCount.
    Return, itemCount.

Teach Angis grab {index:number} from {items:name} to do:
    Run list at with values: items, index: index as pickedItem.
    Return, pickedItem.

Teach Angis check key {key:text} in {value:name} to do:
    Get map has with value: value, key: key as keyExists.
    Return, keyExists.

Teach Angis pack {value:name} to do:
    Turn value into JSON as packedJson.
    Return, packedJson.

Teach Angis unpack demo json to do:
    Parse JSON {"tool": "json", "status": "ready"} as unpackedJson.
    Return, unpackedJson.

Teach Angis make id to do:
    Make uuid as freshId.
    Return, freshId.

Teach Angis seal {message:text} to do:
    Hash text message with sha256 as sealedText.
    Return, sealedText.

Teach Angis clean secrets from {message:text} to do:
    Redact secrets in text message as cleanText.
    Return, cleanText.

Teach Angis flip fate to do:
    Flip coin as fate.
    Return, fate.

Teach Angis square root of {value:number} to do:
    Calculate square root of value as rootValue.
    Return, rootValue.

Teach Angis clamp {value:number} from {low:number} to {high:number} to do:
    Tell math to clamp with value: value, min: low, max: high as clampedValue.
    Return, clampedValue.

Teach Angis what time to do:
    Get current time as flowTime.
    Return, flowTime.

Teach Angis what Angis cant do yet to do:
    Show, "Angis only understands parser phrases or phrases you define."
    Show, "It is not a full Python, C, or JavaScript replacement yet."
    Show, "Low-level systems, drivers, kernels, compilers, advanced networking, and native apps still need host languages or libraries."
    Show, "Some features need installed Python packages like pygame, OpenGL, databases, or other imports."
    Show, "The Apps copy is newer than the Desktop copy and supports more natural Teach Angis flow."
    Show, "Vague wording needs a phrase definition."
    Show, "The package ecosystem is not mature like npm or pip."
    Show, "Unknown APIs need a bridge or import."
    Show, "Apps and games are prototype-level."
    Show, "3D exists, but not like Unity or Unreal."
    Show, "Browser and web deployment are limited, not a full React or Next.js stack."
    Show, "Security and permissions are basic, not a hardened sandbox."
    Show, "Errors and IDE tooling are not as mature as mainstream languages."
    Show, "Some phrase-slot edge cases still need fixes."
    Show, "The honest limit is that Angis can be taught almost any wording, but not every capability is native yet."
    Show, "For deep system work, production web stacks, advanced engines, or unknown APIs, it still needs interpreter work or Python library bridges."
    Show, "Deep systems work, production web stacks, advanced engines, and unknown APIs still need interpreter work or Python/library bridges."
    Show, "It does not have a mature package manager, dependency resolver, lockfile workflow, or public package registry yet."
    Show, "It does not have full production web framework features like routing, SSR, hydration, bundling, auth, migrations, or deployment adapters."
    Show, "It does not have native mobile app builds for iOS or Android."
    Show, "It does not have mature desktop app packaging for every operating system."
    Show, "It does not have advanced game engine systems like physics pipelines, animation graphs, asset importers, shaders, replication, or editor tooling."
    Show, "It does not have a full static type checker, language server, autocomplete engine, formatter, or refactoring engine."
